<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16402" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Eurypylus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐρύπυλος</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Hercules and king of the island of Cos</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				7, 363</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Eurypy-lis</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f., adj., <i>Eurypylan</i>, <b>poet.</b> i. q.
				<i>Coan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">textura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 5, 23.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Son of Euaemon of Thessaly</i>, <i>and
				leader of a body of troops before Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13,
				357</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2, 114</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				97</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 2, 16, 38</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
